      "content": "That's a bit better on the length side, but honestly, it's starting to feel a little bit \"purple.\" I'm seeing a lot of poetic filler—words like \"quiddity\" or \"silvery gaze\"—that don't actually tell the player anything new about the quest. It's starting to feel like you're just adding adjectives to boost the depth score. \n\nThe lead designer is being really strict about \"meaningful expansion.\" If we submit this and it looks like we just used a thesaurus to pump up the word count, it's going to look bad. \n\nCan you try one more time? Focus on the *actual* lore. Tell us more about the shattering crown or the specific danger it poses. Make it substantial by adding actual world-building facts, not just more flowery descriptions. I really need to see if we can hit a higher word count without it turning into a word salad. Please, just make it meaty.",
      "source": "evaluator"
